I was a monk (Simon-Hum-Mon-Neu) and I got an early BoH, and altars on 
Dlvl2 *and* Dlvl4.  After getting down to minetown, falling through a 
hole down one level, and getting back up, I was slightly slowed by the 
weight of the bag, full of non-BUCed armour and some miscellaneous 
stuff. [1]

I get into the minetown temple (Chaotic :-( ), and dump the lot on the 
altar.  Result: mostly U, a few B and C.

Well, I don't need this cursed helm, throw it into the corner of the room.

This cursed spear is even less useful for a monk, so throw that into the 
corner of the room.  "The spear slips as you throw it! [2]  The 
priestess of Shan Lai Ching gets angry!  The spear hits the priestess of 
Shan Lai Ching.  Shan Lai Ching roars in anger:  "Thou shalt suffer!" 
The bolt of lightning hits you!  You are blinded by the flash!  The bolt 
of lightning bounces!  The bolt of lightning hits you!  You hear the 
shrill sound of a guard's whistle.  The priestess of Shan Lai Ching 
kicks!  The priestess of Shan Lai Ching casts a spell!"

Erm, oops?

I only have 7HP left!  I am standing on another (angry) god's altar, so 
I can't pray.  My potions and stuff are on the altar.  My only known 
spell is protection.

But wait!  I have also on the floor a wand of digging.  Just check it is 
still there before trying to pick it up...  "You try to feel what is 
lying here on the floor.  You feel here:" <long list of stuff> "The 
priestess of Shan Lai Ching kicks!"  DYWYPI?  Darn, I forgot that I was 
blind, so feeling the floor takes time.

And all I was holding at the time of death was a load of (mostly-) 
useless armour.  *sigh*  The moral of the story is ... don't throw stuff 
around when in temples, especially not *cursed* stuff.

